00:02:57,644 --> 00:02:58,774
In other words,

437
00:02:58,774 --> 00:03:01,694
the 42" CRT on the first floor

438
00:03:01,694 --> 00:03:04,194
just happens to function as the lifter.

439
00:03:04,194 --> 00:03:06,784
So we were only able to send

440
00:03:06,784 --> 00:03:11,204
D-mail when the studio was open and the TV was on...

441
00:03:11,574 --> 00:03:13,164
That makes a lot of sense!

442
00:03:13,164 --> 00:03:15,914
Don't be so loud. It hurts my head...

443
00:03:15,914 --> 00:03:16,874
Are you okay?

444
00:03:16,874 --> 00:03:19,294
Mr. Braun...

445
00:03:20,164 --> 00:03:22,384
I never thought you would resort to violence.

446
00:03:22,384 --> 00:03:24,924
In a way, it's your own fault.

447
00:03:24,924 --> 00:03:27,634
You're the one who wanted to run an experiment!

448
00:03:28,464 --> 00:03:31,514
Anyway, we almost completely understand

449
00:03:31,514 --> 00:03:33,054
how the Phone Microwave works now.

450
00:03:33,894 --> 00:03:35,054
Which means that next...

451
00:03:35,354 --> 00:03:38,854
We should consider physically transporting an object through time.

452
00:03:38,854 --> 00:03:39,684
Impossible.

453
00:03:39,684 --> 00:03:41,234
Don't dismiss it so quickly!

454
00:03:41,734 --> 00:03:44,524
It's going to end up jelly, no matter what we do.

455
00:03:44,524 --> 00:03:48,074
And how the heck do you fit a human into 36 bytes...

456
00:03:51,454 --> 00:03:53,034
Is this really the time for showing off?

457
00:03:53,034 --> 00:03:55,164
Why would I want to show off to you?

458
00:03:55,164 --> 00:03:56,834
Look at the title of my paper.

