1380
00:04:50,214 --> 00:04:51,054
It's me.

1381
00:04:51,674 --> 00:04:54,384
All the lines have converged at one point.

1382
00:04:54,384 --> 00:04:57,184
The plan will now enter its final stages.

1383
00:04:58,814 --> 00:05:00,774
The goddess who rules the present...

1384
00:05:01,224 --> 00:05:03,184
Begin Operation Verdandi!

1385
00:05:03,604 --> 00:05:04,734
Begin what now?

1386
00:05:04,734 --> 00:05:06,984
Explain what you're talking about a little.

1387
00:05:07,904 --> 00:05:10,784
I'm saying we're going to do that time leap you're talking about.

1388
00:05:10,784 --> 00:05:11,824
Begin now.

1389
00:05:11,824 --> 00:05:15,994
But we'll need a lot of stuff to do it.

1390
00:05:15,994 --> 00:05:21,494
Of course, we only have to read memories stored in the temporal lobe,

1391
00:05:21,494 --> 00:05:24,124
so I think I can get everything in Akiba...

1392
00:05:25,504 --> 00:05:26,504
But...

1393
00:05:27,334 --> 00:05:28,334
What's wrong?

1394
00:05:29,254 --> 00:05:30,884
One problem is that

1395
00:05:30,884 --> 00:05:33,304
I don't think the Phone Microwave will be able

1396
00:05:33,304 --> 00:05:36,134
to sufficiently compress the memory data.

1397
00:05:36,844 --> 00:05:37,974
And...

1398
00:05:38,934 --> 00:05:39,764
What?

1399
00:05:40,604 --> 00:05:42,104
Nothing.

1400
00:05:42,774 --> 00:05:43,734
All right.

1401
00:05:43,734 --> 00:05:46,604
I'll make a list of parts I need for now.

1402
00:05:48,234 --> 00:05:51,154
It's too hard for Mayushii to understand it at all.

1403
00:05:51,154 --> 00:05:54,034
Christina just explained it.

1404
00:05:54,034 --> 00:05:58,034
You're sending your mind, as it exists right now, to the past.

1405
00:06:00,074 --> 00:06:02,334
Sounds scary.

1406
00:06:03,294 --> 00:06:05,794
Is the D-mail not good enough?

1407
00:06:05,794 --> 00:06:09,674
There are too many chaotic variables with the D-mail.

1408
00:06:10,004 --> 00:06:13,884
One message can change things you'd never expect.

1409
00:06:14,964 --> 00:06:17,554
But it's okay to send memories into the past?

1410
00:06:17,554 --> 00:06:20,394
If nothing else, you can

1411
00:06:20,394 --> 00:06:22,814
prevent the past from changing, to a degree.

1412
00:06:23,354 --> 00:06:25,984
You wouldn't have the entire city of Akiba changing...

1413
00:06:26,644 --> 00:06:27,694
The city?

1414
00:06:29,524 --> 00:06:31,154
Nothing, never mind.

1415
00:06:31,154 --> 00:06:32,574
Huh?

1416
00:06:32,574 --> 00:06:34,864
But what happens to you

1417
00:06:34,864 --> 00:06:37,614
after you send your memories?

1418
00:06:37,614 --> 00:06:40,454
Your body is still here, isn't it?

1419
00:06:41,244 --> 00:06:42,454
Well...

1420
00:06:42,454 --> 00:06:47,584
So, Mayushii is talking to Okarin now, right?

1421
00:06:48,504 --> 00:06:51,584
Then, you're saying Mayushii goes back a week,

1422
00:06:51,584 --> 00:06:54,384
and then relives the week, right?

1423
00:06:54,384 --> 00:06:58,884
What happens if she doesn't talk to Okarin this time?

1424
00:06:58,884 --> 00:07:04,014
I assume that you would recall that we spoke,

1425
00:07:04,014 --> 00:07:06,024
but the fact of our having spoken would be erased.

1426
00:07:06,024 --> 00:07:10,444
In other words, Mayushii would remember us talking,

1427
00:07:10,444 --> 00:07:13,234
but Okarin wouldn't?

1428
00:07:13,984 --> 00:07:15,534
I'd imagine so.

1429
00:07:15,534 --> 00:07:19,454
Then, that's kind of sad.

1430
00:07:21,914 --> 00:07:22,534
For me?

1431
00:07:23,624 --> 00:07:24,624
Nope.

1432
00:07:26,744 --> 00:07:28,254
For Mayushii.

1433
00:07:29,164 --> 00:07:31,584
It's Moeka-san!

1434
00:07:31,584 --> 00:07:33,504
Moeka-san!

1435
00:07:46,014 --> 00:07:50,104
You look rather unhappy, Shining Finger.

1436
00:07:56,484 --> 00:07:58,444
"Did you get rid of the time machine?"

1437
00:07:58,444 --> 00:08:00,574
We're still using it.

1438
00:08:00,574 --> 00:08:03,824
And now, we might be able to do a time leapâ

1439
00:08:03,824 --> 00:08:05,454
Don't tell her about that!

1440
00:08:06,744 --> 00:08:09,414
But Moeka-san's a lab member, too, right?

1441
00:08:09,414 --> 00:08:11,664
She is, but...

1442
00:08:13,044 --> 00:08:14,794
"What's a time leap?"

1443
00:08:16,384 --> 00:08:18,004
Just what it sounds like!

1444
00:08:18,004 --> 00:08:20,634
We can send memories through time.

1445
00:08:20,634 --> 00:08:21,844
Memories...

1446
00:08:24,474 --> 00:08:26,054
Moeka-san?

1447
00:08:30,984 --> 00:08:32,604
Moeka-san!

1448
00:08:33,314 --> 00:08:35,234
Is she okay?

1449
00:08:39,284 --> 00:08:42,654
It would be faster to head for Akibaoo first, I guess?

1450
00:08:42,654 --> 00:08:44,034
Mayuri-oneechan!

1451
00:08:47,204 --> 00:08:49,664
It's Nae-chan!

1452
00:08:49,664 --> 00:08:50,914
What's wrong?

1453
00:08:50,914 --> 00:08:52,584
Yo.

1454
00:08:52,584 --> 00:08:54,294
You're still dressed like that?

1455
00:08:56,004 --> 00:08:59,424
The boss told me to stay this way all day.

1456
00:08:59,424 --> 00:09:01,514
You'll poison children's minds.

1457
00:09:01,514 --> 00:09:02,264
Poison?

1458
00:09:02,264 --> 00:09:05,094
I'm careful never to walk around with poison.

1459
00:09:05,094 --> 00:09:06,054
Huh?

1460
00:09:06,054 --> 00:09:08,434
Anyway, Nae said she wanted to

1461
00:09:08,434 --> 00:09:11,604
talk to Okabe Rintarou, so we were looking for you.

1462
00:09:12,144 --> 00:09:12,894
To me?

1463
00:09:14,944 --> 00:09:16,274
I'm sorry!

1464
00:09:16,274 --> 00:09:18,944
My dad was really mean back there!

1465
00:09:19,324 --> 00:09:20,614
Nae-chan...

1466
00:09:20,614 --> 00:09:22,694
You came all this way to say that?

1467
00:09:22,694 --> 00:09:25,034
What a well-trained little pet.

1468
00:09:25,034 --> 00:09:27,204
She's not a pet.

1469
00:09:27,994 --> 00:09:29,334
Don't worry.

1470
00:09:29,334 --> 00:09:32,124
I cause trouble for Mr. Braun all the time.

1471
00:09:32,504 --> 00:09:33,204
We're even.

1472
00:09:34,874 --> 00:09:37,674
That's not like the Okabe Rintarou I know...

1473
00:09:38,754 --> 00:09:40,884
Okarin's always like this.

1474
00:09:42,924 --> 00:09:45,514
Mayushii's gonna get going, okay?

1475
00:09:46,184 --> 00:09:47,054
Meeting someone?

1476
00:09:47,054 --> 00:09:47,764
Yup!

1477
00:09:47,764 --> 00:09:50,854
I'm going to give the cosplayer, Fubuki-chan, her outfit.

1478
00:09:50,854 --> 00:09:52,644
Come to think of it, it's almost time for Comima.

1479
00:09:52,934 --> 00:09:53,604
Yup.

1480
00:09:53,604 --> 00:09:54,604
Bye!

1481
00:09:54,604 --> 00:09:56,274
See you, Suzu-san and Nae-chan!

1482
00:09:57,694 --> 00:09:58,774
See you!

1483
00:09:59,774 --> 00:10:01,944
Okay, let's head back ourselves.

1484
00:10:01,944 --> 00:10:05,824
No, I need to find the parts Christina asked me for.

1485
00:10:08,284 --> 00:10:12,034
Makise Kurisu works with SERN.

1486
00:10:23,384 --> 00:10:24,884
<i>A SERN spy?</i>

1487
00:10:26,134 --> 00:10:27,264
<i>No way.</i>

1488
00:10:33,394 --> 00:10:34,224
All your base are...

1489
00:10:34,224 --> 00:10:35,064
...belong to us.

1490
00:10:38,854 --> 00:10:40,104
You can't sneak up on me!

1491
00:10:40,104 --> 00:10:40,944
It's against the rules!

1492
00:10:41,654 --> 00:10:44,154
So, you were posting on @channel.

1493
00:10:44,944 --> 00:10:48,494
I realized you were an @channeler a long time ago.

1494
00:10:45,784 --> 00:10:47,454
I wasn't, no...

1495
00:10:48,494 --> 00:10:49,414
No!

1496
00:10:49,414 --> 00:10:51,954
There's no point in hiding it now.

1497
00:10:52,704 --> 00:10:54,164
This sucks...

1498
00:10:54,164 --> 00:10:55,124
All right.

1499
00:10:55,124 --> 00:10:56,254
From now on,

1500
00:10:56,254 --> 00:10:58,414
I officially give you the title of Channeler...

1501
00:10:58,414 --> 00:11:00,834
Don't give me any more weird nicknames!

1502
00:11:00,834 --> 00:11:02,794
And please, keep this a secret!

1503
00:11:02,794 --> 00:11:03,754
Why?

1504
00:11:04,254 --> 00:11:06,804
You could list it on your resume.

1505
00:11:06,804 --> 00:11:10,054
If they knew a serious academic were posting,

1506
00:11:10,054 --> 00:11:12,014
they'd probably make a few threads about you.

1507
00:11:12,014 --> 00:11:13,434
Why would I care?

1508
00:11:13,434 --> 00:11:17,484
Then what? You'd sage them?

1509
00:11:18,734 --> 00:11:21,234
I hate myself for understanding that last sentence.

1510
00:11:21,234 --> 00:11:23,114
Either way, I feel better.

1511
00:11:23,114 --> 00:11:23,944
I can't imagine

1512
00:11:23,944 --> 00:11:27,114
anyone who's so terrible at hiding things

1513
00:11:27,114 --> 00:11:28,444
being a spy.

1514
00:11:29,244 --> 00:11:30,034
What does that mean?

1515
00:11:30,404 --> 00:11:34,994
The part-time warrior said you were a SERN spy.

1516
00:11:34,994 --> 00:11:37,124
What is that supposed to mean?

1517
00:11:37,704 --> 00:11:39,374
That's impossible.

1518
00:11:39,374 --> 00:11:40,714
Indeed.

1519
00:11:41,714 --> 00:11:45,004
You're an agent the Organization sent,

1520
00:11:45,004 --> 00:11:48,554
who's had a change of heart and now works as my assistant.

1521
00:11:48,554 --> 00:11:49,634
That's not true, either.

1522
00:11:49,634 --> 00:11:52,514
So how's the work going?

1523
00:11:52,514 --> 00:11:53,094
Work?

1524
00:11:53,724 --> 00:11:55,014
The time leap.

1525
00:11:55,014 --> 00:11:56,764
I bought all the parts.

1526
00:11:56,764 --> 00:11:59,064
Oh... That's right.

1527
00:11:59,064 --> 00:12:00,604
I should make it, shouldn't I?

1528
00:12:01,734 --> 00:12:03,314
I've come this far.

1529
00:12:03,314 --> 00:12:05,274
What is this?

1530
00:12:05,904 --> 00:12:07,274
You're getting scared?

1531
00:12:07,274 --> 00:12:08,984
That, too...

1532
00:12:08,984 --> 00:12:12,704
I keep asking myself what will happen if we really make it.

1533
00:12:13,324 --> 00:12:15,244
But more than that...

1534
00:12:16,124 --> 00:12:17,124
What?

1535
00:12:17,124 --> 00:12:19,204
I should tell you...

1536
00:12:19,204 --> 00:12:21,664
It seems like it's half-obvious already.

1537
00:12:25,584 --> 00:12:27,504
I can't do it here!

1538
00:12:27,504 --> 00:12:29,424
Let's go somewhere I can't see your face.

1539
00:12:32,904 --> 00:12:34,914


1540
00:12:33,184 --> 00:12:38,314
I've got a problem with my dad...

1541
00:12:38,314 --> 00:12:41,184
So your father was struck by lightning,

1542
00:12:41,184 --> 00:12:43,314
on the grassy plains of Arkansas, and fell to the dark sideâ

1543
00:12:43,314 --> 00:12:45,234
If you're going to be a jerk, I'm not telling you.

1544
00:12:45,234 --> 00:12:47,484
All right. Tell me.

1545
00:12:48,194 --> 00:12:51,114
To put it simply, my dad doesn't like me.

1546
00:12:51,944 --> 00:12:54,204
No... He hates me.

1547
00:12:54,824 --> 00:12:59,294
And not as his daughter. As a scientist, as a rival.

1548
00:13:00,044 --> 00:13:03,164
My dad was a physicist.

1549
00:13:03,164 --> 00:13:05,084
I always liked hearing him

1550
00:13:05,084 --> 00:13:08,794
talk about the details of his work.

1551
00:13:09,344 --> 00:13:11,844
And so, by the end of elementary school,

1552
00:13:11,844 --> 00:13:14,224
I could understand his papers.

1553
00:13:16,224 --> 00:13:19,014
And then, I started writing my own papers,

1554
00:13:19,014 --> 00:13:20,644
and winning awards.

1555
00:13:22,394 --> 00:13:24,774
But I didn't care about the awards.

1556
00:13:24,774 --> 00:13:27,864
I loved debating with my father.

1557
00:13:28,734 --> 00:13:31,234
We exchanged papers by e-mail,

1558
00:13:31,234 --> 00:13:32,904
and our debates got deeper.

1559
00:13:33,744 --> 00:13:34,784
But...

1560
00:13:35,994 --> 00:13:39,334
Eventually, my dad stopped debating with me.

1561
00:13:40,454 --> 00:13:42,794
While I enjoyed the debates,

1562
00:13:42,794 --> 00:13:44,834
I was also winning them.

1563
00:13:46,544 --> 00:13:48,714
I pointed out mistakes he'd made,

1564
00:13:48,714 --> 00:13:52,884
and without even thinking about it, I hurt his pride.

1565
00:13:55,764 --> 00:13:57,974
My dad started taking it out on my mom.

1566
00:13:58,514 --> 00:13:59,644
He lost confidence,

1567
00:13:59,644 --> 00:14:02,104
and began withdrawing from his academic peers.

1568
00:14:03,354 --> 00:14:05,234
The last time I saw him,

1569
00:14:05,234 --> 00:14:07,194
he said this to me...

1570
00:14:08,104 --> 00:14:10,274
"Do you pity me?

1571
00:14:10,274 --> 00:14:11,694
Do you look down on me?"

1572
00:14:13,114 --> 00:14:15,114
"You're my daughter. How dare you."

1573
00:14:22,954 --> 00:14:27,004
If I make a device that enables a time leap,

1574
00:14:27,004 --> 00:14:30,044
I think my dad might go insane.

1575
00:14:30,044 --> 00:14:31,504
Even more than before...

1576
00:14:31,504 --> 00:14:34,174
So that's why you're hesitant to make it?

1577
00:14:34,174 --> 00:14:35,594
But don't worry.

1578
00:14:35,594 --> 00:14:38,594
I'll end up doing it, regardless.

1579
00:14:38,594 --> 00:14:40,804
Just like you said, I love experimenting.

1580
00:14:41,304 --> 00:14:44,394
If I see a possibility, I have to investigate it.

1581
00:14:45,474 --> 00:14:47,184
Just like my dad used to...

1582
00:14:48,894 --> 00:14:50,734
The time I spent with my dad...

1583
00:14:52,064 --> 00:14:53,274
...was like that.

1584
00:15:05,794 --> 00:15:10,294
Then we begin Operation Verdandi immediately!

1585
00:15:10,294 --> 00:15:11,714
There's no time to waste!

1586
00:15:11,714 --> 00:15:14,884
The Organization stands at our very doorstep!

1587
00:15:14,884 --> 00:15:16,424
That's your response?

1588
00:15:16,424 --> 00:15:17,884
Of course...

1589
00:15:17,884 --> 00:15:19,554
I am Hououin Kyouma.

1590
00:15:19,554 --> 00:15:22,514
I have a destiny to change the world!

1591
00:15:23,604 --> 00:15:25,354
I shouldn't have said anything...

1592
00:15:25,354 --> 00:15:27,684
And we'll reconcile you with your dad, too!

1593
00:15:27,684 --> 00:15:29,444
Where is he?

1594
00:15:29,944 --> 00:15:31,354
H-He's in Aomori.

1595
00:15:31,354 --> 00:15:34,274
We'll need money to go...

1596
00:15:34,274 --> 00:15:35,524
When you work out the time,

1597
00:15:35,524 --> 00:15:37,484
tell me as soon as you can.

1598
00:15:37,484 --> 00:15:40,204
You can't mean to go with me.

1599
00:15:40,204 --> 00:15:41,414
Naturally!

1600
00:15:41,744 --> 00:15:46,914
I need you in peak mental condition, 
so you can further my ambitions!

1601
00:15:47,544 --> 00:15:50,004
I, Hououin Kyouma, shall accompany you.

1602
00:15:50,004 --> 00:15:53,384
And I shall use my masterful people skills

1603
00:15:53,384 --> 00:15:56,174
to reunite father and daughter.

1604
00:15:56,174 --> 00:15:57,884
What?

1605
00:15:57,884 --> 00:16:00,804
You're a self-proclaimed mad scientist, right?

1606
00:16:00,804 --> 00:16:03,054
Since when do mad scientists have people skills?

1607
00:16:03,054 --> 00:16:05,644
Well, um, you see...

1608
00:16:07,264 --> 00:16:08,474
Why are you laughing?

1609
00:16:09,064 --> 00:16:11,644
Sometimes you're a good guy, you know?

1610
00:16:11,644 --> 00:16:13,314
That's the problem.

1611
00:16:13,314 --> 00:16:16,324
Now that you understand my greatness, back to work.

1612
00:16:17,234 --> 00:16:17,984
Right, right!

1613
00:16:17,984 --> 00:16:20,364
Just so we're clear, this is now decided.

1614
00:16:20,364 --> 00:16:22,454
So I'm dragging you with me, whether you want to go or not!

1615
00:16:24,784 --> 00:16:26,494
Sounds good to me.

1616
00:16:33,424 --> 00:16:35,254
Mayuri-chan?

1617
00:16:36,544 --> 00:16:39,054
What's with all this stuff?

1618
00:16:39,054 --> 00:16:41,974
Shouldn't you call that Okarin guy?

1619
00:16:41,974 --> 00:16:43,634
It's okay...

1620
00:16:44,304 --> 00:16:46,644
I'm almost there.

1621
00:16:47,684 --> 00:16:49,184
Look at the label!

1622
00:16:49,184 --> 00:16:51,314
It says "Makise" right here!

1623
00:16:51,314 --> 00:16:53,854
It reads "Makise pudding."

1624
00:16:53,854 --> 00:16:55,024
That's just a brand name,

1625
00:16:55,024 --> 00:16:57,024
like Morinaga pudding or Koiwai pudding.

1626
00:16:57,024 --> 00:16:58,404
Don't play stupid!

1627
00:16:58,404 --> 00:17:00,154
Who's "Makise," anyway?

1628
00:17:00,154 --> 00:17:01,364
That's my name!

1629
00:17:01,364 --> 00:17:03,284
"Christina Makise"?

1630
00:17:03,284 --> 00:17:06,164
If only you'd written "Christina" instead,

1631
00:17:06,164 --> 00:17:08,874
I wouldn't have accidentally ingested the extra calories.

1632
00:17:09,204 --> 00:17:11,044
Don't eat other people's food!

1633
00:17:11,044 --> 00:17:14,124
And that's my spoon! Don't use it!

1634
00:17:14,124 --> 00:17:17,794
You use the lab's forks, don't you?!

1635
00:17:18,344 --> 00:17:19,294
I'm here...

1636
00:17:21,884 --> 00:17:23,264
What's all that?

1637
00:17:23,264 --> 00:17:26,934
Mayushii's cosplay materials and sleepover set!

1638
00:17:27,434 --> 00:17:28,514
Sleepover?

1639
00:17:29,184 --> 00:17:30,354
Yup!

1640
00:17:30,354 --> 00:17:32,474
I'm going to make some cosplay outfits for Comima.

1641
00:17:32,474 --> 00:17:34,854
Are you sure?

1642
00:17:34,854 --> 00:17:36,024
What about your parents?

1643
00:17:36,024 --> 00:17:37,774
I told them about it.

1644
00:17:37,774 --> 00:17:39,694
You're staying over, too, right?

1645
00:17:39,694 --> 00:17:41,404
To work on the Phone Microwave?

1646
00:17:42,034 --> 00:17:45,244
Yeah, I thought I might.

1647
00:17:45,244 --> 00:17:47,914
But it's kind of depressing to be here.

1648
00:17:47,914 --> 00:17:49,324
There's this Hououin something guy

1649
00:17:49,324 --> 00:17:51,414
who goes around eating people's pudding.

1650
00:17:52,204 --> 00:17:53,914
It's Hououin Kyouma!

1651
00:17:53,914 --> 00:17:55,294
Learn my name, already!

1652
00:17:55,294 --> 00:17:56,754
You're the last person I want to hear that from!

1653
00:17:56,754 --> 00:17:58,754
And don't ignore the part about the pudding!

1654
00:17:58,754 --> 00:18:00,754
Maybe I should leave?

1655
00:18:01,344 --> 00:18:03,964
No, I'll stay,

1656
00:18:03,964 --> 00:18:05,924
but if I do, then Okabe should leave.

1657
00:18:06,724 --> 00:18:08,264
What?!

1658
00:18:08,264 --> 00:18:11,054
The lab is the house of my soul!

1659
00:18:11,054 --> 00:18:12,184
I could never leaveâ

1660
00:18:14,564 --> 00:18:17,854
Why is her condition for staying that I go shopping?

1661
00:18:17,854 --> 00:18:19,354
Come to think of it,

1662
00:18:19,354 --> 00:18:21,654
I've been running errands for my assistant since yesterday.

1663
00:18:24,574 --> 00:18:25,994
Christina?

1664
00:18:26,264 --> 00:18:29,014
From: Assistant 
Subject: I demand compensation and an apology 
 I demand two puddings, 
as punishment for the one you ate. And... 
We're taking a late bus to Aomori, 
due to finances.

1665
00:18:30,624 --> 00:18:32,494
"What are you so happy about?

1666
00:18:32,494 --> 00:18:35,754
Don't forget your role as a lab member."

1667
00:18:38,834 --> 00:18:40,834
I'm not happy, stupid!

1668
00:18:41,754 --> 00:18:42,634
What?

1669
00:18:43,174 --> 00:18:44,924
It's nothing!

1670
00:18:44,924 --> 00:18:48,094
Let's get in, before Okabe gets back.

1671
00:18:48,094 --> 00:18:49,134
Okay.

1672
00:18:55,314 --> 00:18:56,394
My assistant again?

1673
00:18:58,954 --> 00:19:00,254
You know too much.

1674
00:18:58,954 --> 00:19:00,254
You know too much.

1675
